"""RPKI tags only where the IXP ASN fits a standard community

Revision ID: b7d3f2a9c615
Revises: 8c2e5d1a9f47
Create Date: 2026-10-16

A standard community carries a 16-bit ASN, so an IXP with a four-byte ASN cannot
emit (rsasn, 65012) or (rsasn, 65023) and BIRD rejects the whole config. Those
IXPs keep discarding invalid routes and skip the valid and unknown tags, as they
already skip the peer type community

Only rows identical to the previous default set change; edited templates are
reported and left as they are

"""

